      Formatted Input: Which of the following parts of a plant cell has a function that is most similar to the function of an animal skeleton?
A. cell membrane
B. cell wall
C. chloroplast
D. nucleus
        Answer:            **B. Cell Wall**

The cell wall of a plant cell provides structural support, which is similar to the function of an animal skeleton. This similarity arises from both components having the property of providing structural integrity and support for the organism's overall structure. The cell wall acts as a rigid layer outside the cell membrane, giving shape and protection to the cell, much like how an animal skeleton serves as a framework for the body.
